---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Visa">
	<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">Student Visa for Germany</h1>
	<p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">What the German student visa actually involves — the process, and what to expect.</p>

	<!-- Overview -->
	<section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">General Overview</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Once you've secured admission at a German university, the next step is applying for a
			<strong> study visa</strong> to enter Germany. This is done through the consular services
			portal of your designated German consulate — either the <strong>German Embassy in
			Islamabad</strong> or the <strong>German Consulate General in Karachi</strong>, depending
			on where you're from.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			As a general rule, applicants from <strong>Sindh and Balochistan</strong> apply through the
			Karachi consulate, while applicants from <strong>Punjab, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,
			Gilgit-Baltistan, and Azad Jammu &amp; Kashmir</strong> apply through the Islamabad embassy.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-800">
			<strong>Important:</strong> Visa appointment waiting times are usually long, so start your
			application as early as possible and have everything ready in advance.
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Application Process -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Application Process</h2>
		<ol class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-slate-600">
			<li><strong>1. Create an account</strong> on the consular services portal of your designated consulate.</li>
			<li><strong>2. Complete and submit your application</strong>, then join the waiting list.</li>
			<li><strong>3. Wait to be notified.</strong> Waiting times vary and can take a while, so patience is key here.</li>
			<li><strong>4. Document verification.</strong> Once the embassy verifies your submitted documents, they'll send you a link to book your appointment.</li>
			<li><strong>5. Attend your appointment</strong> at your designated consulate on the scheduled date.</li>
			<li><strong>6. Wait for the decision</strong> on your visa application.</li>
		</ol>
		<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-800">
			<strong>Note:</strong> Visa requirements and processing times can change. Always confirm
			current details on your designated consulate's official website before applying.
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>